<title>GERMANY: Lamfalussy - money supply must always be watched.</title>
<headline>Lamfalussy - money supply must always be watched.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>President of the European Monetary Institute, Alexandre Lamfalussy, said on Friday that money supply must always be watched closely after monetary union, whatever monetary policy strategy the future European Central Bank adopts.</p>
<p>He added that money demand would remain uncertain in the euro area of stage three of monetary union.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy was speaking at a press conference to launch the policy document of the European Central Bank, which will operate monetary policy after EMU.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
